From 7963b0ef63714ac30c26cae64e0de012162bc4b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:10:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings, VideoRenderers, windowing/gbm: the finer gamut
 mapping table as an expert setting

System > Display, "Dolby Vision engine", for experts: "Finer gamut mapping"
(videoscreen.hadesdvgamutfine), off by default. On, the bridge asks for
the finer gamut mapping table (dvbridge_render_set_gamut_table()): native
output reads it when it starts (CDVEngineSettings, and its line in
kodi.log), and a bridge for output as HDR10 or for a mapping to SDR when it
is made (ConversionFineGamut()), as the composition is read. kodi.log says
which table a mapping took when that changes
(CDVBridgeGLES::LogGamutTable(), from LogNotes()): its size, its format
and its memory, with a warning where the finer one could not be made and
the standard one is used, and where the graphics chip filters no format
for the table and libplacebo maps the gamut by saturation (which cannot
happen where the bridge runs: it requires OES_texture_float_linear, and
libplacebo-9950 keeps the table in 32-bit floats there).

The strings in English (core #39230, #39231) and in Spanish (es_es, es_ar,
es_mx) in Estuary (#31755, #31756, CGUIDialogSettingsBase).
